  <!-- BCM Philosophy Section -->
  <section id="bcm-philosophy">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="text-center">BCM Philosophy: Two Paths in Crisis</h2>
      <p class="section-subtitle text-center">
        Crises are inevitable. The question is not IF, but WHEN. Organizations face a critical choice.
      </p>

      <div class="comparison">
        <div class="comparison-box without">
          <h3>WITHOUT BCM: Fragile</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>No clear plan when crisis hits</li>
            <li>Confusion and delays</li>
            <li>Improvisation under pressure</li>
            <li>Services disrupted</li>
            <li>Patients unable to access care</li>
            <li>Staff overwhelmed</li>
            <li>Community loses trust</li>
            <li>Lives at risk</li>
            <li>Long, costly recovery</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="comparison-box with">
          <h3>WITH BCM / ISO 22301: Resilient</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Plan activated immediately</li>
            <li>Trained response team</li>
            <li>Clear procedures</li>
            <li>Services maintained</li>
            <li>Critical care continues</li>
            <li>Patients receive treatment</li>
            <li>Staff protected and supported</li>
            <li>Community reassured</li>
            <li>Rapid recovery and learning</li>
            <li>Organization becomes stronger</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-alt mt-2">
        <h3 class="text-center">Core Philosophy</h3>
        <p class="text-center" style="max-width: 800px; margin: 1rem auto;">
          <strong>Preparedness is not optional.</strong> It's our professional responsibility to the communities we serve.
          BCM provides systematic preparation. ISO 22301 provides the proven international framework.
          Recovery costs for unprepared organizations far exceed preparation investment.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Key Benefits Section -->
  <section id="benefits">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="text-center">Key Benefits</h2>
      <p class="section-subtitle text-center">
        Comprehensive platform combining AI intelligence with ISO 22301 compliance
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-3">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>AI-Powered Automation</h3>
          <p>14 specialized AI agents automate BIA analysis, risk assessment, plan generation, and compliance tracking. Multi-model LLM orchestration with RAG for knowledge retrieval.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>ISO 22301 Compliance</h3>
          <p>Complete coverage of all ISO 22301 clauses through 21 platform services. Automated compliance monitoring, gap analysis, and audit trail generation.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>Event-Driven Architecture</h3>
          <p>Real-time event processing with Redis/RabbitMQ EventBus. Pattern detection, anomaly alerts, and automated response workflows for incident management.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>Predictive Intelligence</h3>
          <p>Risk forecasting using Monte Carlo simulation, scenario modeling, and ML-based pattern recognition. Proactive threat detection and mitigation recommendations.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>Living Documentation</h3>
          <p>AI-powered documentation that evolves with your organization. Automatic updates, personalized views, and context-aware examples generated in real-time.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>Community Intelligence</h3>
          <p>Peer learning network with privacy-preserving collective intelligence. Share anonymized patterns, learn from similar organizations, benchmark performance.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The Continuous Resilience Cycle -->
  <section id="resilience-cycle">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="text-center">The Continuous Resilience Cycle</h2>
      <p class="section-subtitle text-center">
        BCM is not a one-time project - it's a living system that strengthens your organization with every cycle
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-4">
        <div class="card">
          <h3 class="text-primary">1. PREPARE</h3>
          <ul style="margin-top: 1rem; color: var(--medium-text);">
            <li>Identify critical services</li>
            <li>Assess risks</li>
            <li>Build response plans</li>
            <li>Train staff</li>
            <li>Test procedures</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3 class="text-primary">2. READY STATE</h3>
          <ul style="margin-top: 1rem; color: var(--medium-text);">
            <li>Continuous monitoring</li>
            <li>Early warning systems</li>
            <li>Plans accessible</li>
            <li>Team ready</li>
            <li>Threat detection</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3 class="text-secondary">3. RESPOND</h3>
          <ul style="margin-top: 1rem; color: var(--medium-text);">
            <li>Activate plan immediately</li>
            <li>Deploy response teams</li>
            <li>Protect critical services</li>
            <li>Support staff</li>
            <li>Communicate clearly</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3 class="text-secondary">4. RECOVER</h3>
          <ul style="margin-top: 1rem; color: var(--medium-text);">
            <li>Restore services</li>
            <li>Return to normal</li>
            <li>Support staff recovery</li>
            <li>Stabilize operations</li>
            <li>Document learnings</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-alt mt-2 text-center">
        <h3>5. LEARN</h3>
        <p style="max-width: 600px; margin: 1rem auto; color: var(--medium-text);">
          What worked well? What needs improvement? Update plans based on real experience.
          Share knowledge across the organization. Each crisis makes the system stronger.
        </p>
        <p style="font-weight: 600; color: var(--primary-color);">
          Then PREPARE again - but now STRONGER with new knowledge
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Platform Layers Overview -->
  <section id="platform-overview">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="text-center">4-Layer Platform Architecture</h2>
      <p class="section-subtitle text-center">
        Modular, scalable architecture designed for enterprise resilience
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-4">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Layer 1: Infrastructure</h3>
          <p><strong>Foundation Services</strong></p>
          <ul style="margin-top: 0.5rem; color: var(--medium-text); font-size: 0.9rem;">
            <li>PostgreSQL (Supabase)</li>
            <li>Redis Cache</li>
            <li>RabbitMQ EventBus</li>
            <li>Qdrant Vector DB</li>
            <li>Prometheus + Grafana</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>Layer 2: Platform Services</h3>
          <p><strong>21 Microservices</strong></p>
          <ul style="margin-top: 0.5rem; color: var(--medium-text); font-size: 0.9rem;">
            <li>BIA Service</li>
            <li>Risk Assessment</li>
            <li>Compliance Tracking</li>
            <li>Plans Management</li>
            <li>+ 17 more services</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>Layer 3: Intelligent Core</h3>
          <p><strong>17 AI Modules</strong></p>
          <ul style="margin-top: 0.5rem; color: var(--medium-text); font-size: 0.9rem;">
            <li>AI Foundation</li>
            <li>Workflow Intelligence</li>
            <li>Expertise Center (14 specialists)</li>
            <li>Predictive Analytics</li>
            <li>+ 13 more modules</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>Layer 4: Interface</h3>
          <p><strong>User Experience</strong></p>
          <ul style="margin-top: 0.5rem; color: var(--medium-text); font-size: 0.9rem;">
            <li>Next.js 14 Web App</li>
            <li>API Gateway</li>
            <li>Admin Panel</li>
            <li>Real-time WebSocket</li>
            <li>Mobile Responsive</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="text-center mt-2">
        <a href="architecture.html" class="btn btn-primary">Explore Full Architecture</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

